WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:05.330 line:10%
 The narrative

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:06.920 line:10%
for the presidential campaign

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.180 line:10%
flipped on Friday

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.140 line:10%
after the president's

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:10.910 line:10%
positive COVID test.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:12.230 line:10%
Now the Trump campaign

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:14.180 line:10%
has shifted to virtual events,

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.580 line:10%
while Joe Biden hits the trail.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.110 line:10%
Joining us now from Minneapolis,

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:19.550 line:10%
Senator Amy Klobuchar,

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:20.940 line:10%
a key backer of the former vice

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:21.740 line:10%
president.

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:24.470 line:10%
Senator, what are your thoughts

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.510 line:10%
about the president's illness?

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:27.510 line:10%
First of all, the fact

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:28.310 line:10%
that the president

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:30.240 line:10%
and first lady have contracted

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:31.220 line:10%
COVID.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:33.740 line:10%
And secondly, how he's handled

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.550 line:10%
COVID over these last months.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:40.130 line:10%
 Well first, Chris, my prayers

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.090 line:10%
are with the president

00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.500 line:10%
and the first lady,

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.450 line:10%
and all of their staff,

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:45.890 line:10%
and the Republican senators

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:48.560 line:10%
that we are we now know are ill.

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:49.670 line:10%
And we wish them all

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.050 line:10%
a speedy recovery.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.940 line:10%
I think it was Joe Biden that

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.490 line:10%
said that this should be not

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.690 line:10%
about partisanship, not

00:00:56.690 --> 00:00:57.530 line:10%
about politics,

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.690 line:10%
this is an American moment.

00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:01.910 line:10%
And to me that means electing

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:04.400 line:10%
a president that has a plan

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.720 line:10%
instead of pandemonium.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:07.490 line:10%
I think it means putting

00:01:07.490 --> 00:01:09.330 line:10%
a strong leader in place that,

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:10.130 line:10%
number one,

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.270 line:10%
understands we listen

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.110 line:10%
to the experts.

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:13.820 line:10%
Just like the doctor you just

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:15.230 line:10%
had on who was telling people

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:16.700 line:10%
yes, wear masks

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.120 line:10%
in public settings.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.060 line:10%
By the way it'll save 100,000

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:22.640 line:10%
lives in 100 days.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.100 line:10%
You need a plan for having

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.050 line:10%
a national testing strategy,

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:28.340 line:10%
which would help us immensely

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:29.780 line:10%
with our economy

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:32.180 line:10%
so businesses can reopen

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.010 line:10%
in a very consistent way.

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:35.270 line:10%
And then the third thing

00:01:35.270 --> 00:01:37.190 line:10%
is transparency with contact

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.410 line:10%
tracing and the like.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:40.970 line:10%
And we just haven't seen that.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:42.260 line:10%
We've heard things like oh, this

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:43.700 line:10%
will be done by Easter.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.690 line:10%
Oh, this will go away

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:45.890 line:10%
with warm weather.

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:47.640 line:10%
Oh, this is a hoax.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.720 line:10%
This is deeply personal to me,

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:49.520 line:10%
Chris.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:50.320 line:10%
You know that.

00:01:50.320 --> 00:01:52.040 line:10%
My husband was very, very sick.

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.380 line:10%
Had pneumonia.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.800 line:10%
Was in the hospital for nearly

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.000 line:10%
a week.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.220 line:10%
And it is deeply personal to so

00:01:58.220 --> 00:01:59.390 line:10%
many Americans, it is now

00:01:59.390 --> 00:02:01.230 line:10%
personal to the president.

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:03.110 line:10%
But it is deeply personal to so

00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:04.260 line:10%
many people.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.230 line:10%
And that's why I think you see

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.520 line:10%
in states like Florida

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:10.669 line:10%
now since the debate, where

00:02:10.669 --> 00:02:11.870 line:10%
people didn't like what they

00:02:11.870 --> 00:02:13.410 line:10%
heard from the president.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.930 line:10%
Joe Biden is up five points

00:02:14.930 --> 00:02:15.980 line:10%
in a poll yesterday.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.960 line:10%
Or he's up in Pennsylvania.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.210 line:10%
Clearly Democrats, Republicans,

00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:22.550 line:10%
and Independents want someone

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:24.260 line:10%
that is following the facts,

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:25.970 line:10%
and is going to help them out

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:26.960 line:10%
and their families,

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:27.760 line:10%
and get us

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.780 line:10%
through this pandemic.

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:31.790 line:10%
 Senator, the Biden campaign

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.410 line:10%
has taken down all

00:02:33.410 --> 00:02:34.770 line:10%
of its negative ads.

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.350 line:10%
But the president--

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:37.610 line:10%
some Republicans

00:02:37.610 --> 00:02:38.960 line:10%
are saying that Democrats are

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.600 line:10%
still attacking the president

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:43.340 line:10%
while he's now in the hospital.

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.240 line:10%
Should discussions about COVID

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.040 line:10%
be

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:47.510 line:10%
off-limits at this particular

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:49.080 line:10%
point?

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.320 line:10%
 Well, not discussions

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.120 line:10%
about COVID.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.430 line:10%
Not when you had seven million

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:55.440 line:10%
people get this virus.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.790 line:10%
Not when you have people in

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.830 line:10%
assisted living who have been

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.050 line:10%
isolated for this entire year.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.610 line:10%
And moms juggling their kids

00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.420 line:10%
on their laps

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:04.320 line:10%
while they're trying to do

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:05.280 line:10%
their work.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:06.360 line:10%
Uh, no.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.920 line:10%
But I think Joe Biden has set

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:08.890 line:10%
the tone here, because he's

00:03:08.890 --> 00:03:09.690 line:10%
a leader.

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.100 line:10%
And he said, look.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.660 line:10%
I want the president to be back.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.070 line:10%
He wants to debate him more.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:15.780 line:10%
He wants him to have

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.280 line:10%
a speedy recovery.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.110 line:10%
And so this isn't about politics

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.160 line:10%
or partisanship.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.660 line:10%
But certainly the pandemic,

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:22.980 line:10%
the effect that it's had

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:24.420 line:10%
on people's lives,

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.010 line:10%
how they have miscalculated

00:03:26.010 --> 00:03:27.540 line:10%
at this administration,

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.130 line:10%
of course that's on the table.

00:03:29.130 --> 00:03:30.690 line:10%
Because as Joe pointed out

00:03:30.690 --> 00:03:33.000 line:10%
at the debate, we have 200,000

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.950 line:10%
families right now that have

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.180 line:10%
a chair at the table that's

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:37.140 line:10%
empty.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:38.370 line:10%
So it is on the table.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:39.490 line:10%
As well as the economy,

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:40.290 line:10%
and how we can get

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:41.760 line:10%
through the day after tomorrow.

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:42.810 line:10%
And the kind of leadership

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.320 line:10%
you'll need to make sure we get

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.120 line:10%
there.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.350 line:10%
 Right.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:49.350 line:10%
The issue of how to campaign

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:50.820 line:10%
during a pandemic

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.830 line:10%
came up during Tuesday's debate.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.930 line:10%
Take a look, Senator.

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.960 line:10%
 And I'll have 25,000, 35,000

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.290 line:10%
people show up at airports.

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:00.090 line:90%
We use airports and--

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:00.180 line:90%
 Are you not--

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:00.410 line:90%
 --hangars, and--

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.140 line:90%
 --worried about the disease--

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.380 line:90%
 --we have a lot of people--

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:02.420 line:90%
 --issues sir?

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.350 line:90%
 Well so far,

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.530 line:90%
we have had no problem

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:05.330 line:90%
whatsoever.

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.140 line:10%
It's outside.

00:04:06.140 --> 00:04:06.940 line:10%
 He's been totally

00:04:06.940 --> 00:04:08.360 line:10%
irresponsible the way in which

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.950 line:10%
he has handled

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.900 line:10%
the social distancing and people

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:12.830 line:10%
wearing a mask.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.090 line:10%
Basically, encouraged them not

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:16.440 line:10%
to.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.870 line:10%
 This raises the whole question

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:21.990 line:10%
of how to reopen the country.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:23.520 line:10%
Whether it's reopening

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:24.500 line:10%
and how you conduct

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:25.300 line:10%
the campaign.

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:26.100 line:10%
Whether it's reopening

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.160 line:10%
the economy.

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.380 line:10%
Whether it's reopening schools.

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.390 line:10%
You just heard Trump campaign

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:33.300 line:10%
advisor, Steve Cortes, say---

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:34.260 line:10%
and the president said

00:04:34.260 --> 00:04:35.250 line:10%
in the debate--

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.460 line:10%
that Joe Biden is being too

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:37.260 line:10%
cautious.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.580 line:10%
Too much of an alarmist.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:41.040 line:10%
And is too ready to shut down

00:04:41.040 --> 00:04:42.670 line:10%
the government again.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.150 line:10%
Or rather, shut down the economy

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:44.950 line:10%
again.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.060 line:10%
Excuse me.

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:47.800 line:10%
 Joe Biden has made it really

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.930 line:10%
clear that he wants to build

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.130 line:10%
back better.

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:52.870 line:10%
And he wants to get this economy

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.640 line:10%
to a place where we're actually

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:55.490 line:10%
expanding.

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:56.290 line:90%
And, in fact, I'd

00:04:56.290 --> 00:04:58.030 line:90%
note that Moody's, not exactly

00:04:58.030 --> 00:04:59.530 line:90%
a liberal organization,

00:04:59.530 --> 00:05:01.090 line:90%
just said that Joe Biden's plan

00:05:01.090 --> 00:05:02.350 line:90%
will add 7 million

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.360 line:90%
more jobs next year than Donald

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.410 line:90%
Trump's plan.

00:05:05.410 --> 00:05:06.610 line:90%
And so he wants to do that.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.320 line:90%
But he believes you use science

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:09.820 line:90%
as a guide, that's all.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.260 line:10%
And you can see you shouldn't

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.510 line:10%
just have testing for White

00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.070 line:10%
House staff.

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:15.940 line:10%
We should be able to have

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.020 line:10%
grocery store clerks,

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:18.400 line:10%
and nurses,

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:19.580 line:10%
and first responders.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:20.920 line:10%
They should be able to have more

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.450 line:10%
frequent testing, too.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.120 line:10%
And there is a way to do this.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:25.810 line:10%
But right now, it's just

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.420 line:10%
this idea that, oh, this is

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:28.220 line:10%
going to get better.

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:29.110 line:10%
We've turned the corner,

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.930 line:10%
as your first guest just said.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.210 line:10%
Thirty-three states, that's

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.010 line:10%
the facts.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:34.120 line:10%
The doctor said them.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:35.680 line:10%
Thirty-three states we've seen

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:37.180 line:10%
increases right now

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.620 line:10%
in the last few weeks.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:40.550 line:10%
And so what that [AUDIO OUT]

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.410 line:10%
into me?

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.000 line:10%
We can get through this.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.410 line:10%
There's so much promising work

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.700 line:10%
being done on vaccines,

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.000 line:10%
but to get to that point

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:47.800 line:10%
we have to have

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:49.600 line:10%
a national testing strategy.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:50.830 line:10%
And then we also have to have

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:53.200 line:10%
an economic plan for what I call

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:54.410 line:10%
the day after tomorrow.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:55.210 line:10%
So we can get

00:05:55.210 --> 00:05:57.690 line:10%
through this stronger.

00:05:57.690 --> 00:05:59.700 line:10%
 Senator, it turns out that two

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:01.350 line:10%
of your Republican colleagues

00:06:01.350 --> 00:06:02.550 line:10%
on the Senate Judiciary

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.770 line:10%
Committee, Senators Mike Lee

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.210 line:10%
and Thom Tillis,

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:07.710 line:10%
have now tested positive

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:08.850 line:10%
for COVID.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:11.100 line:10%
Are Democrats going to try

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:14.220 line:10%
to use this as a way to delay

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.640 line:10%
the confirmation hearing,

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:17.430 line:10%
and the confirmation vote

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:20.640 line:10%
on Judge Barrett?

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.600 line:10%
 It's not a matter of using it,

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:23.400 line:10%
Chris.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.790 line:10%
It happened.

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.170 line:10%
And the first thing we know

00:06:26.170 --> 00:06:26.970 line:10%
is that if you look

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:27.900 line:10%
at the precedent

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.700 line:10%
that Mitch McConnell set,

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.050 line:10%
we should let the people decide.

00:06:31.050 --> 00:06:32.100 line:10%
And that's where the majority

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:32.940 line:10%
of people

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:34.380 line:10%
are when it comes to this.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:36.330 line:10%
Decide who the president is

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:37.470 line:10%
after this election,

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.390 line:10%
and let them pick the nominee.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.130 line:10%
Secondly, we've got the fact

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:42.730 line:10%
that now three senators have it.

00:06:42.730 --> 00:06:43.530 line:10%
As you point out,

00:06:43.530 --> 00:06:44.350 line:10%
two are on the Judiciary

00:06:44.350 --> 00:06:45.870 line:10%
Committee.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:47.760 line:10%
And Mitch McConnell has shut

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:48.960 line:10%
the Senate down for two

00:06:48.960 --> 00:06:50.310 line:10%
[AUDIO OUT]

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:51.990 line:10%
because of health concerns.

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:53.010 line:10%
Because we don't know how many

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.040 line:10%
other Republican senators

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:54.840 line:10%
had it.

00:06:54.840 --> 00:06:55.530 line:10%
There were a number

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:56.330 line:10%
of other ones

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:57.520 line:10%
that were at the Rose Garden.

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.960 line:10%
They have a lunch together where

00:06:58.960 --> 00:06:59.760 line:10%
they don't have masks.

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:00.560 line:10%
We don't do that

00:07:00.560 --> 00:07:01.650 line:10%
on the Democratic side.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:02.710 line:10%
They do.

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.630 line:10%
And so it's very possible

00:07:04.630 --> 00:07:05.430 line:10%
we're going to have more

00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.900 line:10%
senators, more staff.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:07.980 line:10%
So I don't know why you would

00:07:07.980 --> 00:07:09.810 line:10%
ram through the Supreme Court

00:07:09.810 --> 00:07:11.980 line:10%
hearing, put people in danger,

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:12.780 line:10%
because it would be

00:07:12.780 --> 00:07:15.000 line:10%
within that two-week period,

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:16.320 line:10%
while you have shut down

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:17.340 line:10%
the whole Senate.

00:07:17.340 --> 00:07:18.590 line:10%
I just think it's wrong.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:19.860 line:10%
We are suggesting that they

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.370 line:10%
wait.

00:07:22.370 --> 00:07:24.020 line:10%
 But Senator, the fact

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:26.780 line:10%
is that you can hold hearings

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:27.660 line:10%
in different ways.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:30.410 line:10%
In fact, last May, when

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:31.700 line:10%
the chairman of the Judiciary

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.200 line:10%
Committee, Lindsey Graham,

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.850 line:10%
held a virtual hearing,

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.470 line:10%
you very much praised him,

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:38.720 line:10%
and thanked him for doing that.

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.830 line:10%
So you could hold

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.620 line:10%
a virtual hearing for Judge

00:07:42.620 --> 00:07:43.910 line:10%
Barrett.

00:07:43.910 --> 00:07:45.590 line:10%
Which raises the question again,

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.530 line:10%
are you trying to use the fact

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:49.400 line:10%
that there has been

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.140 line:10%
this outbreak, at least

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:53.030 line:10%
three Republican senators,

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:54.890 line:10%
to try to block a nomination

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.160 line:10%
that you frankly oppose

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:56.960 line:10%
fiercely?

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:00.850 line:90%
 Absolutely not.

00:08:00.850 --> 00:08:01.820 line:10%
This is for the highest court

00:08:01.820 --> 00:08:02.620 line:10%
of the land.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:04.090 line:10%
And yes, we have had

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:04.980 line:10%
virtual hearings.

00:08:04.980 --> 00:08:06.440 line:10%
I helped to put them together.

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:07.750 line:10%
It's important to give senators

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:08.740 line:10%
that option.

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:10.240 line:10%
But you want to be able to go

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.410 line:10%
back and forth

00:08:11.410 --> 00:08:12.670 line:10%
with this nominee.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.690 line:10%
Given her views

00:08:13.690 --> 00:08:14.980 line:10%
on the Affordable Care Act,

00:08:14.980 --> 00:08:16.330 line:10%
given that she has clearly

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.740 line:10%
criticized Justice Roberts, who

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:19.540 line:10%
again,

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.760 line:10%
not exactly a blazing liberal,

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.420 line:10%
for upholding the constitutional

00:08:23.420 --> 00:08:24.580 line:10%
of the Affordable Care Act,

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:25.810 line:10%
which allows people to keep

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:27.520 line:10%
their insurance when they've got

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:29.140 line:10%
preexisting conditions.

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:30.470 line:10%
And she has criticized that?

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:31.595 line:10%
Yeah, we want to able

00:08:31.595 --> 00:08:31.940 line:10%
to ask her--

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:32.840 line:10%
 Yeah, but we're doing it.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.880 line:10%
We're doing this virtually,

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:34.680 line:10%
Senator.

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.919 line:10%
We're doing this virtually,

00:08:35.919 --> 00:08:38.020 line:10%
so why can't you question Judge

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:40.090 line:10%
Barrett virtually?

00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:42.030 line:10%
 Again, we believe you should

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:43.900 line:10%
have an in-person hearing.

00:08:43.900 --> 00:08:44.700 line:10%
That doesn't mean

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.200 line:10%
the virtual option wouldn't be

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:47.010 line:10%
available.

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.360 line:10%
But why would you ram--

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:49.590 line:10%
I guess I turned the question

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.120 line:10%
around here, even though you get

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.270 line:10%
to ask the questions.

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:53.130 line:10%
Why would you ram this

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:54.600 line:10%
through when we don't even have

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:56.700 line:10%
a COVID package done to make

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.510 line:10%
sure that people have health

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.310 line:10%
care?

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:01.150 line:10%
That we have the testing

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:02.310 line:10%
I just talked about.

00:09:02.310 --> 00:09:03.210 line:10%
That we have the funding

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.010 line:10%
for that.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.280 line:10%
The Senate Republicans have been

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:07.110 line:10%
resisting this, while Nancy

00:09:07.110 --> 00:09:09.120 line:10%
Pelosi has been valiantly

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:10.200 line:10%
working on it, and the White

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.190 line:10%
House now claims they want

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.030 line:10%
a package.

00:09:12.030 --> 00:09:13.860 line:10%
Why would be doing this

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:15.480 line:10%
instead of actually be helping

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:16.960 line:10%
the American people?

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:18.720 line:10%
So that's why I think it is so

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:19.910 line:10%
important that that's what we

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:20.710 line:10%
do,

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:21.600 line:10%
instead of ramming

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.250 line:10%
through a Supreme Court justice.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.690 line:10%
Wait until after the election.

00:09:24.690 --> 00:09:25.800 line:10%
Better for safety.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:28.680 line:10%
Better for the country.

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:30.210 line:10%
 Senator Klobuchar, thank you.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.010 line:10%
Thanks for your time

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:31.810 line:10%
this weekend.

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:33.200 line:10%
Please come back.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:34.400 line:10%
 I will, and I did that all

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.050 line:10%
without interrupting you once,

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.310 line:10%
I would like to point out, Chris

00:09:37.310 --> 00:09:38.110 line:10%
Wallace.

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:41.573 line:10%
 I interrupted you a couple

00:09:41.573 --> 00:09:42.373 line:10%
of times.

00:09:42.373 --> 00:09:43.460 line:10%
It's a little hard on this Skype

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:44.260 line:10%
deal.

00:09:44.260 --> 00:09:46.030 line:10%
Senator, thank you.

